ects the finalized metering data schema once the\n  GPU usage metering strategy lands — schema drift is absorbed in the\n  consumption layer without changing the reporting API contract.\n- The existing build and test pipeline for the affected repository remains\n  green.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable\n  time ranges computed from the metering data delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990\n  (computation and retrieval half; the administrator viewing surface is\n  delivered by the Dashboard admin view epic).\n- **HLR-2 (P1, bundled)** — CSV export and stable API retrieval for finance\n  tooling, bundled because it is a presentation/transport mode of the same\n  report computation and data structure as HLR-1.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- External timing risk: the metering data schema finalizes only when\n  RHAISTRAT-9990 lands. Work can proceed against the current draft schema with\n  drift absorbed in the consumption layer, but final validation of the report\n  semantics waits on the finalized schema. This timing is externally\n  controlled and is tracked here as a risk, not an acceptance criterion on\n  schedule.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32994,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b25c3f2d1e4e5799","agent_id":"ad501466c5198a39c","session_id":"38385a1f-a4a3-4a7d-b611-f75447628639","uuid":"e1d823a8-b36f-43a2-abc7-7116a4ab638b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:39:37.083Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 into epics"}
