putation in the Dashboard).\n- The view is behind a Dashboard feature flag (OdhDashboardConfig) and is\n  disabled by default.\n- The existing Dashboard build and test pipeline remains green.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — the administrator viewing surface for per-project GPU-hour\n  consumption reports over selectable time ranges (the computation and API\n  half is delivered by the consumption reporting backend epic).\n- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)** — current-month consumption against each project's\n  Kueue quota, bundled because it renders in the same Dashboard admin view\n  surface as the HLR-1 time-range reports; a split would build the same UI\n  surface twice.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The view depends on the reporting API contract from the consumption\n  reporting backend; work on view scaffolding, quota display, and feature\n  flagging can proceed in parallel, but final wiring waits on the stable API.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33785,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b25c3f2d1e4e5799","agent_id":"ad501466c5198a39c","session_id":"38385a1f-a4a3-4a7d-b611-f75447628639","uuid":"bdcb808d-3932-468c-943a-2d420e6d9e42","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:39:47.735Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 into epics"}
