{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-afc8c888606ef95d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n3\ttitle: Per-project GPU-hour consumption reporting backend\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: -1\n16\t  external_dependency: -1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 1\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Per-project GPU-hour consumption reporting backend\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the backend capability that computes per-project GPU-hour\n34\tconsumption reports over selectable time ranges from the metering data\n35\tdelivered by the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990), and exposes\n36\tthose reports through a stable API and CSV export for administrators and\n37\tfinance tooling. It consumes the metering data; it does not re-implement\n38\tmetering collection.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Compute per-project GPU-hour consumption reports aggregated over\n43\t  administrator-selectable time ranges, sourced from the per-project GPU-hour\n44\t  usage data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990).\n45\t- Expose report retrieval through a stable API suitable for finance tooling\n46\t  integration.\n47\t- Provide CSV export of the reports.\n48\t- Keep the metering-schema consumption isolated in the report computation\n49\t  layer so that changes in the (not-yet-final) metering data schema are\n50\t  absorbed there without reworking the reporting API or export surfaces.\n51\t- No metering collection pipeline work (owned by RHAISTRAT-9990) and no\n52\t  currency/cost-rate modelling — reports are denominated in GPU-hours.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Per-project GPU-hour consumption reports can be computed over\n57\t  administrator-selectable time ranges.\n58\t- Reports are computed from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage\n59\t  metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990); no collection logic is re-implemented\n60\t  here.\n61\t- Reports are retrievable via a stable API usable by finance tooling.\n62\t- Reports are exportable as CSV.\n63\t- The consumption layer reflects the finalized metering data schema once the\n64\t  GPU usage metering strategy lands — schema drift is absorbed in the\n65\t  consumption layer without changing the reporting API contract.\n66\t- The existing build and test pipeline for the affected repository remains\n67\t  green.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable\n72\t  time ranges computed from the metering data delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990\n73\t  (computation and retrieval half; the administrator viewing surface is\n74\t  delivered by the Dashboard admin view epic).\n75\t- **HLR-2 (P1, bundled)** — CSV export and stable API retrieval for finance\n76\t  tooling, bundled because it is a presentation/transport mode of the same\n77\t  report computation and data structure as HLR-1.\n78\t\n79\t## Risks / Notes\n80\t\n81\t- External timing risk: the metering data schema finalizes only when\n82\t  RHAISTRAT-9990 lands. Work can proceed against the current draft schema with\n83\t  drift absorbed in the consumption layer, but final validation of the report\n84\t  semantics waits on the finalized schema. This timing is externally\n85\t  controlled and is tracked here as a risk, not an acceptance criterion on\n86\t  schedule.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86a5068c